> Remo Dentato wrote:

> Reviewing what others have written, I will say that the answer is "yes  
> and no", with the technical purist answer being "no".

> At one time Pierre and my wife Nora were working on a generalized  
> word-breakdown algorithm, but the effort stalled out, and I don't know if  
> anyone has worked on such a thing in the last couple of years. Nora's  
> last effort *may* have been satisfactory, but we never found a practical  
> way to test the algorithm, and I think there were open issues left  
> undecided. There is no name for the generalized algorithm (which would  
> break down any text string marked for stress uniquely.


Is the description of the algorithm available somewhere?
I now use a very rough test to check that a "word" can't be broken as a  
CMAVO+BRIVLA and for slinkuhi that it's "Craf3*(gim?$|raf4?y)" but  
not "raf3*(gim?$|raf4?y)", I might get some inspiration by reading Nora &  
Pierre Algorithm.

